---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import CirclePlan from '../components/CirclePlan.astro';
import Notify from '../components/Notify.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Estaleiro"
  description="Estaleiro Liberdade, a Brazilian self-directed entrepreneurship programme from 2012, now being rebuilt in Stockholm with Klustret Ekskäret."
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="page-head">
      <p class="label eyebrow">Estaleiro Liberdade, Porto Alegre 2012</p>
      <h1 class="display estaleiro-title">A school of entrepreneurship through <span class="nowrap">self-knowledge.</span> But pirate.</h1>
      <div class="column prose intro">
        <p class="lede">
          That was the tagline, and it was accurate. Estaleiro Liberdade ran in Porto Alegre from
          2012, in a shared house on Rua Liberdade that several social-impact organisations were
          using at the same time. We started by opening the doors every Friday for free teaching and
          learning sessions. The first cohort of five began in August 2012. By 2014 it had reached
          São Paulo with groups of up to 24.
        </p>
        <p>
          I co-founded it and served as president of the formal organisation. My part ran through
          2015.
        </p>
      </div>
    </header>

    <section class="section first" aria-labelledby="how">
      <h2 id="how">How it worked</h2>
      <div class="column prose">
        <p>
          Journeys ran three to four months. Participants were called sailors, facilitators were
          pirates, and nobody had a curriculum. No grades, no reading lists, no attendance
          requirement. Everything was proposed and nothing was mandatory.
        </p>
        <p>
          Four kinds of gathering: conversation circles, workshops on methods, hands-on sessions on
          your own project, and individual mentoring. The toolkit came from wherever it worked,
          including Nonviolent Communication, design thinking, Dragon Dreaming and agile.
        </p>
        <p>Three principles held it together.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="plan-wrap">
        <CirclePlan />
      </div>

      <div class="column prose">
        <p>
          Before we started, I travelled through Europe visiting multiple schools
          in Europe and being inspired by Kaos Pilot and Knowmads. In 2013 a
          second expedition visited nine more schools, crowdfunded on Catarse. What we found there
          shaped the model.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="out">
      <h2 id="out">What came out of it</h2>
      <div class="column prose">
        <p>
          Small things, mostly, which is what happens when cohorts are a dozen people. Herói Postal
          turned emails into handwritten physical letters, with the income shared with hospitalised
          people who wrote them. One participant left with a writing project he'd been avoiding for
          years and started it. A facilitator built a career transition programme of her own out of
          the experience.
        </p>
        <p>The programme carried on without me for a while and wound down around 2015.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="sthlm">
      <h2 id="sthlm">Stockholm</h2>
      <div class="column prose">
        <p>
          Klustret Ekskäret is a community and coworking space on Odengatan, started in 2016 by
          Stiftelsen Ekskäret, a foundation Tomas Björkman set up in 2008. The foundation runs two
          places: Klustret in the city, and an island in a nature reserve out in the Stockholm
          archipelago. Weekdays Klustret is somewhere to work. Evenings and weekends it turns into
          whatever the members decide to run there.
        </p>
        <p>
          Klustret calls itself a lab and an experiment in self-organisation. Members sit in
          circles, each one responsible for an area, and the whole thing runs on six principles
          about taking responsibility for your own contribution, showing up as you are, sharing what
          you have, acting before you're certain, and everyone being a host rather than a guest.
        </p>
        <p>
          I recognised all of that. Estaleiro ran on rotating leadership, shared responsibility, and
          circle agreements about listening without judgement and treating silence as part of the
          conversation. Different country, different decade, the same bet: people work out what to
          build by working on themselves, in a group that holds them to it.
        </p>
        <p>
          Klustret is also an Inner Development Goals hub. IDG is the vocabulary that didn't exist
          in 2012, when we called it <span lang="pt">autoconhecimento</span> and had to explain it
          every single time.
        </p>
        <p>We're building a version of Estaleiro there. Details when there are details.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="notify-wrap">
        <Notify list="estaleiro" lead="More soon. Leave your email if you want to know when." />
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .eyebrow {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }

  .estaleiro-title {
    max-width: 20ch;
  }

  .nowrap {
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .intro {
    margin-top: var(--space-8);
  }

  .first {
    padding-top: var(--space-8);
  }

  .plan-wrap {
    margin-block: var(--space-12);
  }

  .notify-wrap {
    margin-top: var(--space-8);
  }
</style>
